=== Router rules table ===
- bucket=gpqa_organic_chem
  match: item.subject == 'Organic Chemistry' (GPQA-Diamond)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'stem-max', 'balanced': 'stem-max', 'quality': 'stem-max'}
  finding: stem-max/chem_thinking_gate validated 90.9% mean, 3 seeds, 0.2pt spread (docs/mixture-of-orchestrations-plan.md section 1; the chem_flagship_gate lineage).
- bucket=supergpqa_hard_stem
  match: item.subject in {'Science', 'Engineering'} (SuperGPQA hard-subset disciplines)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'rag_thinking_gate', 'balanced': 'rag_thinking_gate', 'quality': 'flagship_panel'}
  finding: benchmark/results/supergpqa_findings.md: 23% unanimous-wrong, cheap panel -11.6 vs flagship baseline; flagship_panel validated +4.1 mean (3 seeds); rag_stack_findings.md: rag_thinking_gate validated +3.0 mean (3 seeds, never negative), cheaper than flagship_panel.
- bucket=gpqa_hard_stem
  match: item.subject contains 'chem' or 'physic' (case-insensitive; GPQA-Diamond Subdomain/High-level-domain)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'stem-max', 'balanced': 'stem-max', 'quality': 'stem-max'}
  finding: Byte-identical to thinking_gate's validated 3-seed behavior for every non-chemistry subject (stem-max only overrides Organic Chemistry). RAG excluded: rag_r1_findings.md's GPQA tripwire measured retrieval at -4.7 on GPQA-Diamond (search-proof by construction).
- bucket=medicine
  match: item.subject in {'step1', 'step2&3'} (MedQA's only per-row field, the USMLE exam step)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'single-call', 'balanced': 'standard-tribunal', 'quality': 'standard-tribunal'}
  finding: benchmark/results/medqa_findings.md: 4% unanimous-wrong (vs SuperGPQA-hard's 23%), engine ties flagship (+2, inside noise) -- 'a single-call-or-standard-tribunal domain, NOT a flagship_panel domain.'
- bucket=saturated_easy
  match: item.subject in ['biology', 'business', 'computer science', 'economics', 'health', 'history', 'math', 'other', 'philosophy', 'physics', 'psychology'] (exact, case-sensitive; MMLU-Pro category)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'single-call', 'balanced': 'single-call', 'quality': 'single-call'}
  finding: benchmark/results/mmlu_pro_findings.md: flagship baseline 94%, engine -12 overall; per-category breakdown showed these categories 100% baseline=engine (unanimous-and-correct); excludes engineering/chemistry/law, the only categories that regressed in that pilot.
- bucket=unknown
  match: no rule above matched item.subject (including subject=None, e.g. GSM8K/MATH loaders)
  profile_by_budget: {'cheap': 'standard-tribunal', 'balanced': 'thinking_gate', 'quality': 'flagship_panel'}
  finding: Plan section 3's asymmetric-loss principle: bias uncertain classifications toward stronger profiles as budget rises (standard-tribunal -> thinking_gate -> flagship_panel) rather than guessing a cheap route on an undiagnosed domain.
